{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>His own hands shall bring the fire-offerings of YHWH.</b> Since the rest belongs to the owners, this bringing is a Torah decree that the owners give to YHWH everything — the fat and the breast — and the priests earn from the table on high, as it were." "<b>The breast, to wave it.</b> Even though he places the fat upon the breast at the time of waving, nevertheless the principal waving is for the sake of the breast, to make known that it is given to the One on high. The fat, however, is already known to belong to YHWH, since it is offered upon the altar."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:53.229610425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}